	(text "TPS63802 buck-boost -> +3V3 (VOUT = 0.5V*(1+R7/R8) = 3.308V, datasheet Fig. 10-1).\nMODE low = power-save (PFM). Starts from VIN > 1.8V, 11uA Iq.\nUNDERVOLTAGE CUTOFF: EN has a precise threshold (1.10V rising / 1.00V falling), so\nR6/R15 (2.2M/1M) from VSYS turn the rail OFF below ~3.20V and back ON above\n~3.52V (+-3%), ~1.1uA. Backstop only: firmware shuts down gracefully first (~3.4V,\nmeasured via an ADC). The charger does NOT stop over-discharge; the cell\nprotection board is the last line. Footprint: project lib (TI DLA0010A)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 137.16 129.54 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7c02af28-d0ef-5645-9d98-841cac5627f3")
	)
